{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1473428-agg-damage-vs-ballistic","id":1473428,"title":"Agg damage vs ballistic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-27T14:56:50-08:00","id":1473428,"title":"Agg damage vs ballistic","content":"How does ballistic armor interact with aggravated damage. Lets say someone is shooting incendiary ammo at a Vampire wearing armor, or a Werewolf with natural 2/2 armor taking silver bullets, mage with an enchanted agg gun shooting at an officer in SWAT armor, etc.<br /> <br /> Ballistic armor generally downgrades lethal to bashing so this has left players of mind with questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T16:58:18-08:00","id":1473432,"title":"","content":"It comes down to the source of damage and the source of armor. In the case of the vampire wearing ballistic armor it would probably mitigate some of the damage because the armor is preventing some of the fire from reaching the vampire's body. Banes often bypass natural armor entirely. &quot;Silver weapons always deal aggravated damage to werewolves&quot; implies no downgrading is possible. <br /> That said, I would apply the same reasoning to a werewolf wearing a bulletproof vest. A shot that's stopped by the vest means silver never touches flesh, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+